Qdrant 1.13.6 and earlier persist shard keys to disk in an old format. This format has since been replaced due to it having some fundamental problems. Qdrant 1.15.4 and 1.15.5 actively migrate (<https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/7110>) the old format to the new replacement, if the old format is still used. Qdrant 1.16.0 completely removes (<https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/pull/7047>) support for the old format.

In other words: this is relevant if your Qdrant instance is from Qdrant 1.13.6 or earlier and you use shard keys. If you upgrade to Qdrant 1.16.0 without visiting 1.15.4 or 1.15.5 you'll see a panic on startup.

To mitigate this issue in practice I'd recommend any of:
- upgrade to Qdrant 1.15.5 first, then upgrade to Qdrant 1.16.0
- stick with your current version and wait for Qdrant 1.16.1

In our next patch version (Qdrant 1.16.1) I'll make sure to fix this issue. I'll re-enable the old format so that it can load just fine. We expect to release it some time next week.

